    },
    {
      "id": "nZqxH1zdygvu0FqVFiNSI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 8719.548725581066,
      "y": 10490.335695294347,
      "width": 1051.5115966796875,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0d",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 614340861,
      "version": 15,
      "versionNonce": 1397620477,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783309628122,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " - Users search/view for businesses a lot, but they hardly ever leave reviews",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " - Users search/view for businesses a lot, but they hardly ever leave reviews",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RUnz6FLx154iCcLxW72Ul",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10657.876831689564,
      "y": 9281.279978901106,
      "width": 1807.2587890625,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0e",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 427096115,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1101318003,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783309638550,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) How would you efficiently calculate and update the average rating for businesses to ensure it's readily available in search results?",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) How would you efficiently calculate and update the average rating for businesses to ensure it's readily available in search results?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hgfJKoX4tWjBPmzFFUyCa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10687.45617643313,
      "y": 9336.950674366963,
      "width": 1481.2271728515625,
      "height": 70,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0f",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 369312573,
      "version": 11,
      "versionNonce": 379612211,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783309667384,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- We want to show users the average rating of the business since this is often the first thing they look at\n  when deciding on a business to visit.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- We want to show users the average rating of the business since this is often the first thing they look at\n  when deciding on a business to visit.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "IeD1DfiofN1G9NXaY4WsP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10693.002303572548,
      "y": 9429.62443684113,
      "width": 1841.531005859375,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 947994109,
      "version": 241,
      "versionNonce": 1619393971,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783310474645,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Worst Sol:\n  - Join on businesses table and reviews table, expensive query, slows down other read operations on db impacting system performance.\n\n- Better Sol:\n  - Synchronous update with Optimistic Locking\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Worst Sol:\n  - Join on businesses table and reviews table, expensive query, slows down other read operations on db impacting system performance.\n\n- Better Sol:\n  - Synchronous update with Optimistic Locking\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "4o6O5iM6EFqRsOs8mc5RZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10719.489555637285,
      "y": 9611.479900608278,
      "width": 1842.631091358197,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 424832243,
      "version": 118,
      "versionNonce": 1119369533,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783310500648,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- To make the update efficient, we can introduce a new column, num_reviews, into the Business table. \n- Now, to update an average rating, we simple calculate (old_rating * num_reviews + new_rating) / (num_reviews + 1), which is cheap,\njust a few CPU cycles so it can be done synchronously for each new review",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- To make the update efficient, we can introduce a new column, num_reviews, into the Business table. \n- Now, to update an average rating, we simple calculate (old_rating * num_reviews + new_rating) / (num_reviews + 1), which is cheap, just a few CPU cycles so it can be done synchronously for each new review",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OXWK7s0LJRDNVgJYP47GN",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 10665.005469833426,
      "y": 9928.874838278572,
      "width": 953.8684576353307,
      "height": 1606.5152970700306,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "transparent",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1194589885,
      "version": 220,
      "versionNonce": 486898163,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783310927679,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "status": "saved",
      "fileId": "87a25b729ecc365af28528ebcfcb31c6172ed0a3",
      "scale": [
        1,
        1
      ],
      "crop": null
    },
    {
      "id": "50cEkEnQvHwcfv-P1aQeB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10699.198367486128,
      "y": 9762.991451342401,
      "width": 1714.4669189453125,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1536935805,
      "version": 73,
      "versionNonce": 807483635,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783311064669,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Optimistic Lock: The key idea: when you write, check that num_reviews (your \"version\") still matches what you read. \n  If it doesn't, retry the whole read-modify-write cycle.\n- Optimistic locking is great when conflicts are rare — the retry cost is low and you avoid holding locks. \n  But if a business is popular (think: a viral restaurant getting hundreds of reviews per second),  you'll get heavy contention \n  and lots of wasted retries.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Optimistic Lock: The key idea: when you write, check that num_reviews (your \"version\") still matches what you read. \n  If it doesn't, retry the whole read-modify-write cycle.\n- Optimistic locking is great when conflicts are rare — the retry cost is low and you avoid holding locks. \n  But if a business is popular (think: a viral restaurant getting hundreds of reviews per second),  you'll get heavy contention \n  and lots of wasted retries.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lywSuZ_e1h7NUlK7dSl5V",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10990.644460054686,
      "y": 9734.213695286955,
      "width": 11.199996948242188,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
